## Control {{controlId}}: Establish and Enforce Security Configuration Settings for Information Technology Products

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization establishes and enforces security configuration settings within the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant through Intune device configuration profiles and compliance policies managed by {{variables.systemAdministrator}}.

{{#if deviceConfigurationsActive}}
**Security Configuration Enforcement:**
{{deviceConfigurationsCount}} device configuration profiles enforce security settings on managed endpoints:
{{#if configurations}}
{{#each configurations}}
- **{{displayName}}** ({{platformType}}){{#if description}} — {{description}}{{/if}}
{{/each}}
{{/if}}

Configuration profiles enforce settings aligned with DISA STIGs and CIS benchmarks, including firewall rules, antivirus settings, BitLocker encryption, screen lock timeouts, and application restrictions.
{{else}}
Security configuration enforcement has not been confirmed through device configuration profiles.
{{/if}}

{{#if compliancePolicyActive}}
**Compliance Monitoring:**
Intune compliance policy "{{policyName}}" continuously evaluates endpoint configurations against required security settings:
{{#if policies}}
{{#each policies}}
- **{{displayName}}**{{#if description}} — {{description}}{{/if}}
{{/each}}
{{/if}}

Non-compliant devices are automatically blocked from accessing CUI resources via Conditional Access integration, enforcing remediation before access is restored.
{{else}}
Compliance policy enforcement has not been configured. Security configuration drift detection is not active.
{{/if}}

**Responsible Party:** {{variables.systemAdministrator}}

**Verification Method:** Examine Intune configuration profiles, compliance policy reports, non-compliance remediation logs, and STIG/CIS benchmark mapping documentation.

